Translation patch: seal_at and open_json_with of the request-state codec, so that the public
functions seal, seal_with, open_json and open_json_with translate (plan Section 2.3, R09, R10,
R13, R14; human decisions 2026-11-24: targets R09-R15, variant A "minimal Rust change")

Applies to: the copy of upstream origin/main 7caec762799bece6fba38e4298b8ca7db8bac12c after
01-request-state-wire.patch and 02-phase2-tests.patch (scripts/apply-patches.sh applies
formal/trusted/patches/*.patch in file-name order, patch -p1 -F 0, only to the copy in
.llbc/work/; the real source is never patched). File: crates/rmcp/src/model/request_state.rs.
Generated with git diff from the patch-01+02 copy. The patch body below is the authoritative
content. Toolchain measured: Aeneas nightly-2026.11.24-fb44cb4, Charon 0.1.324, Rust
nightly-2026-09-17.

Not part of this patch (they stay in the repository): the Charon settings in
crates/rmcp/Cargo.toml (the exclude entries of seal, seal_with, seal_at, new_with_keyring,
with_rs1_signing, with_rs1_fallback, open_json and open_json_with removed; serde_core moved
from exclude to opaque) and the external models of formal/trusted/Rmcp/. with_rs1_signing,
with_rs1_fallback and new_with_keyring need no source change on this toolchain (measured: they
translate with only their exclude entries removed). seal_json and seal_json_with stay excluded
(blocked upstream: Aeneas does not support the mutually recursive serde_core::ser traits).

Change (non-test lines only; no test is added or changed):
1. seal_at: `let expiry = match options.ttl { .. }` becomes `let ttl = options.ttl;` followed
   by `let expiry = match ttl { .. }`; the match arms are unchanged.
2. open_json_with: `serde_json::from_slice(&payload).map_err(RequestStateError::Deserialization)`
   becomes `match serde_json::from_slice(&payload) { Ok(value) => Ok(value), Err(error) =>
   Err(RequestStateError::Deserialization(error)) }`.

Why each hunk is needed (each measured alone on the patch-01+02 copy, with only the exclude
entries removed):
1. Without hunk 1, Aeneas stops on seal_at with "[Error] Unreachable" at request_state.rs
   lines 531:21-533:21 (the `match options.ttl` expression; interp/Interp.ml line 686), and
   seal and seal_with call seal_at. With hunk 1 alone, seal_at, seal_with and seal translate.
   (Matching on a field read through the shared reference `options` fails; matching on a local
   copy works.)
2. Without hunk 2, Aeneas fails on the FnOnce impl that rustc generates for the enum variant
   constructor RequestStateError::Deserialization used as a function: "[Error] Arrow types are
   not supported yet" and "[Error] Internal error: please file an issue" at request_state.rs
   lines 137:4-137:48. With hunk 2 and serde_core opaque, open_json and open_json_with
   translate; with hunk 2 alone (serde_core excluded) the trait serde_core::de::DeserializeOwned
   of their signatures is missing ("Could not find: trait_decl_id"). A closure
   `|e| RequestStateError::Deserialization(e)` is not used because clippy's redundant_closure
   lint rejects it.
No upstream Aeneas issue has been filed (as of 2026-11-24); minimal reproducers are kept outside
the repository.
With this patch the eight functions seal, seal_with, seal_at, with_rs1_signing,
with_rs1_fallback, open_json, open_json_with and new_with_keyring translate with real bodies,
no sorry is generated, and every earlier block of Funs.lean and Types.lean is unchanged up to
its Source line numbers.

Behaviour:
1. options.ttl is an Option<Duration>, which is Copy: `let ttl = options.ttl;` copies the
   value that the match scrutinee read before, and the match computes the same expression on
   it (0 without a TTL, otherwise now_ms.saturating_add(ttl.as_millis().min(i64::MAX as u128)
   as i64)). No other statement changes.
2. Result::map_err(op) is `match self { Ok(t) => Ok(t), Err(e) => Err(op(e)) }`
   (core/src/result.rs lines 961-969), and op is the variant constructor, so the match returns the same value
   on both paths; the value type T and the error variant are unchanged.
The public API is unchanged. Existing tests that cover the changed lines (all pass on the copy
before and after this patch, with the crate's other library tests in the translated feature
configuration plus macros, 835 in total): for hunk 1 rs1_known_answer_is_unchanged and
rs2_known_answer_matches_wire_specification (byte-exact tokens sealed by seal_at with a 90 s
TTL at a fixed time), within_ttl_opens, past_ttl_is_expired, ttl_and_associated_data_combine,
rs2_roundtrips_with_associated_data_and_ttl, and every seal/seal_with round trip without TTL;
for hunk 2 seal_open_roundtrips_json (Ok path) and
serde_is_reached_only_after_integrity_verification (Err path: invalid JSON gives
RequestStateError::Deserialization).

diff --git a/crates/rmcp/src/model/request_state.rs b/crates/rmcp/src/model/request_state.rs
index 6ccb755..4e93408 100644
--- a/crates/rmcp/src/model/request_state.rs
+++ b/crates/rmcp/src/model/request_state.rs
@@ -524,11 +524,15 @@ impl RequestStateCodec {
         associated_data: &[u8],
     ) -> Result<T, RequestStateError> {
         let payload = self.open_with(sealed, associated_data)?;
-        serde_json::from_slice(&payload).map_err(RequestStateError::Deserialization)
+        match serde_json::from_slice(&payload) {
+            Ok(value) => Ok(value),
+            Err(error) => Err(RequestStateError::Deserialization(error)),
+        }
     }
 
     fn seal_at(&self, payload: &[u8], options: &SealOptions<'_>, now_ms: i64) -> String {
-        let expiry = match options.ttl {
+        let ttl = options.ttl;
+        let expiry = match ttl {
             Some(ttl) => now_ms.saturating_add(ttl.as_millis().min(i64::MAX as u128) as i64),
             None => 0,
         };
